# What the Vercel CLI must not upload. It doesn't read .gitignore, and the
# first attempt shipped 485 MB of local build caches before failing on a
# 100 MB file. The build happens on Vercel, so only the source goes up.
# Anchored with a leading slash where a bare name would also match a
# folder deeper in the tree (lib/content is source and has to go up).
/.next
/.next-*
/.git
/node_modules
/test-results
/playwright-report
/coverage
/docs
/design
/content
/tests
/export
/emulator-data
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
serviceAccountKey.json
*-service-account*.json
.env*
!.env.example
# public/videos is the 1.1 GB symlink to the untouched original recordings
# outside the repo. It must never go up. What DOES go up is
# public/videos-web: the same 36 lessons re-encoded to about 260 MB by
# scripts/compress-videos.mjs, served as ordinary static files by the app.
# They used to live in a Vercel Blob store, which suspended itself for
# going over the free storage allowance and took every recording down with
# it; the app's own static hosting has no separate quota to trip.
/public/videos
!/public/videos-web
